{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '270,320p' test/yang/latte_oracle/h3_3_fixture_family.md; sed -n '585,633p' test/yang/latte_oracle/h3_3_fixture_family.md; sed -n '805,820p' test/yang/latte_oracle/h3_3_fixture_family.md; sed -n '2380,2460p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"  registry shape for this case, and §4.7's fixture observes the effect\n  only through `unparse`, which is insensitive to it for a single\n  registered ident.\n\n## 4. The family\n\nProposed corpus rows are shown in the corpus's EDN shape (A form; the\nharness derives B/C, using `:guest-call` where present). New IDs are\nmarked †. Every predicted A outcome below is A-verified (§0); predicted\nB/C outcomes are the same value unless stated, derived per §3.\n\n### 4.1 defenv predicates\n\nF1† `:h3-3-axiom-true` — primary witness for `axiom?/1` (direct):\n\n```clojure\n{:id :h3-3-axiom-true,\n :call (latte-kernel.defenv/axiom? (latte-kernel.defenv/->Axiom (quote a) [] 0 (quote T)))}\n```\n\nExpected A/B/C: `true`. Required trace: `[gate-defenv-axiom? 1]` in both\nC lanes. The two false companions are refusal rows in §5 (R1); they trace\nthe same record and, negativity notwithstanding, would also credit\n`axiom?/1` under the harness as it stands if they pass (§5.1). F1\nremains the designated primary witness in this design's accounting.\n\nF2† `:h3-3-registered-definition-ambient` — designed witness for\n`registered-definition?/1`, **non-crediting** (§7):\n\n```clojure\n{:id :h3-3-registered-definition-ambient,\n :call (latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? (quote gate-no-such-definition)),\n :guest-call (registered-definition? env (quote gate-no-such-definition))}\n```\n\nExpected A: `false` — the name is in neither the ambient `empty-env`\nnor any namespace the A leg can resolve (the name is chosen to resolve\nnowhere; if a future namespace interns it, this prediction breaks and\nthe fixture must be renamed, never re-expected). Expected B/C: `false`\n(context fetch on the initial context misses both maps). There is no\nrequired trace for credit, because this row credits nothing: its guest\ncall is predicted to trace `[registered-definition? 2]` and\n`[registered-definition? 3]` in both C lanes (§3), but\n`kernel-executed-arity?` for upstream `/1` seeks\n`[gate-defenv-registered-definition? 1]`, no bare-name mapping exists,\nand §7 withdraws the +1 trace-table mapping an earlier draft proposed\n(it is not arity-safe). The gate-wrapper `/1` the direct route would\notherwise use is arity-broken against the context signature (§3), so\nno ordinary fixture credits this arity; the gate stays honestly\n`:blocked` on it. The non-symbol refusal companion is R2 in §5. A `true` case for `/1` is deliberately **not**\ndesigned: on A it could only be produced by namespace resolution (the\n\nF19† `:h3-3-readable-term-3` — primary witness for `readable-term-/3`\n(**named integration**):\n\n```clojure\n{:id :h3-3-readable-term-3,\n :call ((var latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term-) (quote #{x}) (quote {}) (quote (λ [x ✳] [x y]))),\n :guest-call (latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term- (quote #{x}) (quote {}) (quote (λ [x ✳] [x y])))}\n```\n\nExpected A/B/C: `(λ [x' ✳] [x' y])` — the explicit bound map is\nthreaded: the renamed binder is substituted for the bound occurrence,\nthe free `y` is untouched. Required trace:\n`[gate-syntax-readable-term- 3]`; redundant `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]`.\nCredit requires registering `:h3-3-readable-term-3`, as F18.\n\n### 4.7 unparser (side-effecting)\n\nF20† `:h3-3-unregister-unparser` — primary witness for\n`unregister-unparser!/1` (**named integration**; the trace-name mapping\nalready exists, §2):\n\n```clojure\n{:id :h3-3-unregister-unparser, :mode :unparser-install,\n :call (let [_ (latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser! :gate (fn [t] (if (= t (quote x)) [(quote shown) true] [t false])))]\n         [(latte-kernel.unparser/unparse (quote x))\n          (do (latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! :gate)\n              (latte-kernel.unparser/unparse (quote x)))]),\n :guest-call (let [k1 (register-unparser env :gate (fn [t] (if (= t (quote x)) [(quote shown) true] [t false])))]\n               [(unparse k1 (quote x)) (unparse (unregister-unparser k1 :gate) (quote x))])}\n```\n\nExpected A/B/C: `[shown x]` — before removal the registered unparser\nrewrites `x`; after removal it does not. The effect is observed only\nthrough `unparse`, never through the registry value (which holds host\nfunctions upstream and guest closures on C — incomparable evidence by\nconstruction). The A leg runs under `:unparser-install`, so the ambient\natom it mutates is the harness's isolated one; B/C thread the immutable\nregistry through the returned context, and the *prior* context is never\nreused after removal in this row (prior-context preservation for\nregistries is already asserted by the slice-8 registry sequences).\nRequired trace: `[unregister-unparser 2]` in both C lanes; redundant\n`[register-unparser 3]`, `[unparse 2]`. Credit requires registering\n`:h3-3-unregister-unparser` in `kernel-named-integrations`; the\nconservative `:user`-from-`:standard` behavior (§3) is pinned on A by\nthe verification script and must not be \"corrected\" in any row. The\nabsent-ident refusal is R10.\n\n## 5. Refusal and edge companions (all `:negative? true` when integrated)\n- No arity is left without a designed fixture or an explicit note:\n  16 direct + 3 named-integration + 1 non-crediting = 20.\n- Preparation contributes **zero** coverage until reviewed and\n  integrated: nothing in this round changes the checked-in evidence,\n  and the gate remains `:blocked` with 20 unexercised arities.\n\nRedundant (incidental) witnesses, predicted from §3's call graph —\nuseful if a primary trace is missing at integration, never counted\nabove: `binderify/3` also in F4; `beta-reduction/1`, `beta-step/2`,\n`redex?/1` also across F6–F9; `norm/instantiate-def/3` also in F11/F12\n(via `delta-reduction`); `mk-fresh/2`, `mk-fresh/3`,\n`readable-term-/2`, `readable-term-/3` also across F15/F17/F18;\n`parse/2` in F13 (already credited elsewhere).\n\n## 8. Integration sketch and verification (next round, not this one)\n\n     :portability-refusals\n     [{:source '(.getStackTrace exc) :disposition :excluded\n       :reason \"Host stack traces have no portable error-data representation; the compiler refuses the accessor.\"}]\n     :representation-seams\n     {'kind/var? \"JVM Clojure Var predicate; explicitly declared, with no namespace lookup.\"\n      'kind/with-meta \"Pure metadata attachment on the existing host value representation; the data ABI has no metadata-write export.\"}\n     :context-fields {'latte-kernel.proof/+opacity-fn+ :opacity-policy}\n     :fresh-supply-convention\n     {:input {:counter 0} :allocation '(gensym supply prefix)\n      :result '[symbol next-supply]\n      :rebuild-type-result '[original-result next-context]\n      :ambient-prefix-only :refused}\n     :runtime {:clojure (clojure-version) :java (System/getProperty \"java.version\")}\n     :instruction-budget-per-lane 4000000\n     :instruction-budget-note \"The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions. Body-entry stream writes add guest instructions; traced fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound. The harness drains only after halt. Under the D2 record lane the binding fixture's walker cell needs 2,024,912 steps (1.2% over 2M; semantic 1,105,792); the architect's 2026-11-04 ruling approves a uniform 4,000,000 acceptance budget (~1.98x headroom on the binding lane, measurement-supported, no per-fixture table).\"\n     :manifest-bindings (count manifest) :function-arity-candidates (count all-arities)\n     :manifest-functions (count (filter :arities kernel-entries))\n     :admitted-function-arity-count (count admitted-arities)\n     :excluded-function-arity-count (- (count all-arities) (count admitted-arities))\n     :binding-dispositions (frequencies (map :disposition manifest))\n     :admission-note \"Manifest dispositions define the denominator independently of fixture success; excluded bindings retain explicit portability reasons.\"\n     :program-status (if (empty? unexercised) :fixture-closure-complete :execution-evidence-incomplete)\n     :residual-closure kernel-fixture-closure\n     :coverage {:proven-direct-function-arities (vec (sort-by pr-str direct))\n                :exercised-count (count exercised) :unexercised unexercised\n                :entries exercise-entries\n                :named-integration-fixture-ids (vec (sort kernel-named-integrations))\n                :transitive-execution-coverage :recorded-function-arity-body-entry\n                :context-extra-arguments kernel-context-extra-arguments\n                :trace {:record-shape '[guest-function arity]\n                        :transport :explicit-guest-stream :lanes [:c-walker :c-semantic]\n                        :point :selected-arity-body-entry}\n                :basis \"Passing direct calls or named integrations must record the exact function/arity executing in both C lanes. Static closure membership never counts; full branch coverage is not required.\"\n                :inventory inventory}\n     :recorded-portability-boundaries\n     (mapv #(select-keys % [:id :status :recorded-deviation])\n           (filter #(= :recorded-deviation (:status %)) results))\n     :recorded-upstream-failures\n     (mapv #(select-keys % [:id :status :recorded-upstream-failure])\n           (filter #(= :recorded-upstream-failure (:status %)) results))\n     :counts (frequencies (map :status results)) :fixture-count (count results)\n     :negative-fixture-count (count (filter :negative? results))\n     :dependency-graph\n     (into (sorted-map)\n           (for [[fname source] kernel-sources]\n             [fname (vec (sort (filter (set (keys kernel-sources)) (walk-symbols source))))]))\n     :fixtures results}))\n\n\n(defn write-kernel-gate-evidence!\n  \"Explicit evidence/coverage refresh; normal tests never update these files.\n   With `dir`, writes into that directory (the round-trip test's temp dir);\n   without it, the checked-in locations.\"\n  ([] (write-kernel-gate-evidence! \"test/yang/latte_oracle\"))\n  ([dir]\n   (let [evidence (kernel-gate-evidence)]\n     (spit (str dir \"/slice9_unexercised.edn\")\n           (str \";; GENERATED from exact execution evidence in both C lanes.\\n\"\n                (pr-str (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (pr-str %1) (pr-str %2)))\n                              (for [entry (get-in evidence [:coverage :entries])\n                                    :when (= :unexercised (:exercise entry))]\n                                [(:function-arity entry) (:missing-dependency entry)]))) \"\\n\"))\n     (with-open [w (io/writer (str dir \"/slice9_evidence.edn\"))]\n       ;; prn keeps (quote ...) in valid EDN rather than pprint's reader\n       ;; shorthand. One fixture per line keeps refreshes independently diffable.\n       (binding [*out* w *print-length* nil *print-level* nil]\n         (print \"{\")\n         (doseq [[k v] (dissoc evidence :fixtures)] (pr k) (print \" \") (prn v))\n         (println \":fixtures [\")\n         (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)] (prn row))\n         (println \"]}\")))\n     (select-keys evidence [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates :coverage]))))\n\n\n(deftest test-kernel-differential-gate\n  (let [evidence (kernel-gate-evidence)]\n    (is (= (count (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus)) (count (set (map :id (:fixtures evidence)))))\n        \"Every named fixture runs exactly once, including negatives\")\n    (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)\n            :when (and (:negative? row) (= :completed (get-in row [:a :status])))\n            :let [outcome (get-in row [:a :outcome]) value (:value outcome)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
